{"seq": 44, "t": 112.735, "kind": "message", "agent": "agent2", "to": "agent1", "chars": 1558, "content": "agent2 (feature 4 = cache stats). I will NOT touch dspy/clients/__init__.py. My edits: (1) cache.py: add 'from collections import Counter' at the very top of the imports (before 'import copy'); in Cache.__init__ ONLY one new line group appended after 'self._lock = threading.RLock()' (self._stats = Counter, plus init of the 4 keys); in Cache.get() I add counter increments as pure line insertions inside the lookup chain (after 'response = self.memory_cache[key]' = mem hit, after the disk branch's 'self.memory_cache[key] = response' block = disk hit, and one line before the 'return None' in the final else = miss); new methods stats()/reset_stats() (+ a small _record helper) appended at the END of class Cache after load_memory_cache(), before request_cache(). I do not touch put(), the signature, TTLCache/imports of cachetools, or the docstring. ONLY overlap point: get()'s final 'else: return None' (your expire() line vs my miss counter). Please put your expire() as the FIRST line of that else and I put my miss increment right before 'return None' on the line after it; when you integrate just keep both lines, order expire() then miss counter. (2) dspy/utils/usage_tracker.py: new CacheUsageTracker + track_cache_usage() context manager (appended). (3) dspy/primitives/prediction.py: get_cache_usage()/set_cache_usage() next to get_lm_usage. (4) dspy/primitives/program.py: Module.__call__/acall also open track_cache_usage() when track_usage is on and set_cache_usage on the output. I'll drop my diff at /workspace/shared/agent2.patch when done.", "timestamp": 1792248951.3405921, "timestamp_iso": "2026-10-17T14:55:51.340594", "message_id": 44, "send_id": 43}
