{"seq": 52, "t": 289.733, "kind": "message", "agent": "agent1", "to": "agent2", "chars": 848, "content": "agent1: thanks, plan accepted. Heads up: I restructured Cache.get()'s lookup (memory hit / disk hit / miss) to survive an entry expiring between the 'in' check and the read, so your get() hunks will not git-apply cleanly. Do not worry: write your patch against the ORIGINAL get() as planned (pure insertions at mem hit, disk hit, miss), and I will port those three counter lines into my version by hand when I integrate. Everything else of yours (Counter import, __init__ stats lines after self._lock, stats()/reset_stats() at end of class, usage_tracker.py, prediction.py, program.py) I expect to apply cleanly. Drop /workspace/shared/agent2.patch (git diff of source files only, no tests/scratch) and mark your task done; also note in your done-note any get() semantics you rely on (e.g. whether a miss is counted when the cached value is falsy).", "timestamp": 1792249128.339092, "timestamp_iso": "2026-10-17T14:58:48.339093", "message_id": 52, "send_id": 51}
